    "q-47240": {
      "dom_id": "step-q47240",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Evaluate $\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2})+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e).$",
      "worked_solution": "The natural logarithm reverses the action of the exponent. The principle is:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{x})=x\n$$\n\nIn the first and second term, we have $x=2$ and $x=1,$ respectively. Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2})=2 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(e)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2})+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e)=2+2\\cdot 1=4\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-47240-a",
