    "q-99683": {
      "dom_id": "step-q99683",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "$\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{3})}{9}=$",
      "worked_solution": "The natural logarithm reverses the action of the exponent. The principle is:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{x})=x\n$$\n\nIn our case,  we have $x=3.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{3})}{9}=\\frac{3}{9}=\\frac{1}{3}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
