      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Rounded to $3$ decimal places,  $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{10})=$",
      "worked_solution": "We compute the required expression to $3$ decimal places using a calculator, rounding the intermediate step to $6$ decimal places to avoid rounding error. This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{10}) & ≈\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3.162\\,278) \\\\  & ≈1.151\\end{aligned}\n$$",
